@startuml allocation_cost_estimation_service
title Allocation cost estimation service -- LLM is display-only; planner stays heuristic; snapshot at submit (revised)

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam BackgroundColor white
skinparam classBackgroundColor #fafafa
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype polyline

legend top right
  | <#fef3c7> | EXISTING (shipped, unchanged) |
  | <#bbf7d0> | PLANNED -- new file/class/column |
  | <#bfdbfe> | PLANNED -- modified |
  | <#fecaca> | External (Postgres / Firestore / disk) |
endlegend

' ============================================================
' Scope rule (Path B):
'   * cost_for_dry_run (pre-render preview)
'       -> calls the LLM on cache miss; stores formula
'       -> result shown to the user before submit
'   * confirm-upload (submit boundary)                << NEW >>
'       -> server re-runs cost_for_dry_run (cache hit
'          guaranteed since pre-render just ran)
'       -> stamps the total on render_groups.pre_render_cost_estimate_usd
'   * plan_initial / plan_retry (render flow)
'       -> NEVER touch the LLM; allocation decisions stay
'          on the deterministic heuristic
'       -> jobs.estimated_cost_usd remains heuristic-derived
'          (used internally for allocation scoring only)
'   * UI ESTIMATED COST during render
'       -> reads the render-group snapshot when present;
'          falls back to SUM(jobs.estimated_cost_usd) for
'          legacy groups submitted before this change
'   * actual bill -> measured telemetry (TaskActualCost), unchanged
' ============================================================

' ============================================================
' MODULE: serverV2/allocation/services/allocation_cost_estimation_service
' (UNCHANGED from current production state -- shown for context)
' ============================================================
package "serverV2/allocation/services/allocation_cost_estimation_service" <<Frame>> #e0f2fe {

  package "(value object -- frozen formula + math)" <<Rectangle>> #fef3c7 {
    class AllocationCostFileFormula <<existing>> {
      + base_seconds_per_frame_at_anchor : float
      + samples_exponent : float
      + resolution_exponent : float
      + denoise_overhead_seconds : float
      + engine : str
      + notes : str
      + llm_provider : str
      + llm_model : str
      --
      + seconds_per_frame(samples, resolution_pct, denoise) : float
    }
  }

  package "(cache + hasher)" <<Rectangle>> #fef3c7 {
    class AllocationCostFileFormulaRepository <<existing>> {
      + get(heaviness) : AllocationCostFileFormula | None
      + put(heaviness, formula)
    }
  }

  package "(LLM call)" <<Rectangle>> #fef3c7 {
    class AllocationCostLLMCaller <<existing>> {
      + call(heaviness) : AllocationCostFileFormula
    }
  }

  package "(orchestrator -- module entry)" <<Rectangle>> #fef3c7 {
    class AllocationCostEstimationService <<existing>> {
      + base_seconds_per_frame_at_anchor(heaviness) : float
        ' Pre-render path -- may call LLM on cache miss.
        ' Applies safety_multiplier.  NOT called from
        ' the render flow.
      + is_enabled() : bool
        ' config/cost_estimation.cost_estimator_enabled
    }
  }
}

' ============================================================
' Existing touchpoints (already shipped)
' ============================================================
package "serverV2/allocation" <<Frame>> #e0f2fe {
  class AllocationLLMClient <<existing>> #fef3c7 {
    + chat(provider_name, request) : LLMChatResponse
  }

  class AllocationCostEstimationConfigRepository <<existing>> #fef3c7 {
    Reads ``config/cost_estimation`` doc.
    Fields: cost_estimator_enabled, provider_name,
    model, safety_multiplier.
  }

  class allocation_time_analyzer <<existing>> #fef3c7 {
    Reads ``heaviness["llm_base_seconds_at_anchor"]``
    if present; otherwise runs the heuristic.
    UNCHANGED for Path B -- only the pre-render path
    populates the override field, so render-flow calls
    continue running the heuristic.
  }
}

package "serverV2/allocation/services/allocation_planning_service" <<Frame>> #e0f2fe {
  class AllocationPlanningService <<modified>> #bfdbfe {
    Constructor unchanged (already takes
    ``cost_estimation_service``).
    --
    cost_for_dry_run() -- UNCHANGED:
      LLM enrichment on this path stays.  Returns the
      same GroupCostEstimate today's pre-render UI consumes.

    plan_initial() + plan_retry() -- UNCHANGED:
      No LLM, no cache read.  Pure heuristic allocation.
      Stamps heuristic-based ``estimated_seconds`` /
      ``estimated_cost_usd`` on each PlannedTask (used
      internally for allocation scoring + chunk sizing).

    cost_for_committed_jobs() -- MODIFIED:
      NEW signature: takes ``snapshot_usd : float | None``
      and the existing ``rows : list[dict]``.
      If ``snapshot_usd`` is non-None -> build a
      GroupCostEstimate whose ``total_cost_usd`` is the
      snapshot (chunks still come from rows for the
      per-fleet breakdown the UI shows).
      Else -> existing behaviour (SUM jobs.estimated_cost_usd).
  }
}

' ============================================================
' NEW touchpoints for Path B
' ============================================================
package "serverV2/services/render_groups" <<Frame>> #e0f2fe {
  class RenderGroupService <<modified>> #bfdbfe {
    Constructor gains:
      allocation_client : AllocationClient
        (already injected today for other calls --
         just reuse the dry-run cost surface here).
    --
    confirm_upload() -- NEW step at the end:
      1. Resolved scene + frame plan + priority are
         already in scope (the heuristic-side estimate
         already runs here).
      2. Call allocation_client.cost_estimate_for_dry_run(
             resolved scene, frame plan, priority)
         -- this hits the LLM-eligible path; the formula
         cache populated 0.5s ago by the pre-render call
         means no LLM API call fires.
      3. Stamp the resulting ``total_cost_usd`` on
         ``render_groups.pre_render_cost_estimate_usd``
         via the repository (below).
      Idempotent: safe to re-run; the value just
      overwrites.
  }
}

package "serverV2/repositories" <<Frame>> #e0f2fe {
  class RenderGroupRepository <<modified>> #bfdbfe {
    + set_pre_render_cost_estimate_usd(
        group_id : str,
        value : float,
      )                                                   << new method >>
    + get_pre_render_cost_estimate_usd(
        group_id : str,
      ) : float | None                                     << new method >>
    ' Plus one read-path tweak: list/detail SELECTs
    ' include the new column so callers can read it
    ' without an extra query.
  }
}

package "serverV2/allocation" <<Frame>> #e0f2fe {
  class AllocationFacade <<modified>> #bfdbfe {
    cost_estimate_for_committed_group() -- MODIFIED:
      Today: rows = job_repo.list_for_group(group_id);
             return planning.cost_for_committed_jobs(rows).
      New:   snapshot = group_repo.get_pre_render_cost_estimate_usd(group_id);
             rows = job_repo.list_for_group(group_id);
             return planning.cost_for_committed_jobs(
                 rows, snapshot_usd=snapshot,
             ).
  }
}

package "serverV2/infrastructure" <<Frame>> #e0f2fe {
  class "db.init_db()" as DbInit <<modified>> #bfdbfe {
    Append one idempotent ALTER TABLE:
      ALTER TABLE render_groups
        ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS
          pre_render_cost_estimate_usd DOUBLE PRECISION
    Legacy groups (pre-this-change) have NULL -- the
    facade's read-path treats NULL as "no snapshot,
    fall back to SUM(jobs)".
  }
}

' ============================================================
' Externals
' ============================================================
package "Postgres" <<Frame>> #fecaca {
  class "allocation_cost_file_formulas" as PgFormulas <<existing>> {
    UNCHANGED.  Formula cache populated by pre-render
    LLM call; read by the confirm-upload re-run
    (always a cache hit in the normal flow).
  }

  class "render_groups (new column)" as PgRenderGroups <<modified>> #bfdbfe {
    pre_render_cost_estimate_usd
      DOUBLE PRECISION                          << NEW >>
    Per group, the LLM-derived projection
    captured at submit.  Frozen for the life
    of the group -- retries do NOT update it.
  }

  class "jobs" as PgJobs <<existing>> #fef3c7 {
    estimated_cost_usd (heuristic-derived,
    used internally for allocation scoring;
    summed only as a fallback for legacy
    groups without a snapshot)
  }
}

package "Firestore: config/global" <<Frame>> #fef3c7 {
  class "config/cost_estimation doc" as FirestoreLlm <<existing>> {
    cost_estimator_enabled
    provider_name
    model
    safety_multiplier
  }
}

' ============================================================
' Caller-side flow markers
' ============================================================
package "serverV2/services/pre_render" <<Frame>> #e0f2fe {
  class PreRenderEstimator <<existing>> #fef3c7 {
    Unchanged.  Calls
    orchestrator.cost_estimate_for_dry_run(...)
    -- this is the LLM-eligible path; populates
    the formula cache as a side-effect.
  }
}

package "serverV2/allocation render flow" <<Frame>> #e0f2fe {
  class AllocationPendingTickProcessor <<existing>> #fef3c7 {
    Unchanged.  Calls plan_initial -- pure
    heuristic; NEVER touches the LLM or the
    formula cache.
  }

  class RetryExecutor <<existing>> #fef3c7 {
    Unchanged.  Drives plan_retry -- pure
    heuristic; NEVER touches the LLM or the
    formula cache.
  }
}

' ============================================================
' Relationships
' ============================================================
AllocationCostEstimationService --> AllocationCostFileFormulaRepository : get / put
AllocationCostEstimationService --> AllocationCostLLMCaller : call() on miss
AllocationCostEstimationService --> AllocationCostEstimationConfigRepository : safety_multiplier + enabled

AllocationCostLLMCaller --> AllocationLLMClient : chat()

AllocationCostFileFormulaRepository --> PgFormulas : SELECT / UPSERT
AllocationCostEstimationConfigRepository --> FirestoreLlm : reads

PreRenderEstimator ..> AllocationPlanningService : cost_for_dry_run (LLM-eligible)
AllocationPlanningService ..> AllocationCostEstimationService : cost_for_dry_run path only
allocation_time_analyzer ..> AllocationPlanningService : reads enriched heaviness on the dry-run path

RenderGroupService ..> AllocationPlanningService : cost_for_dry_run at confirm (cache hit)
RenderGroupService --> RenderGroupRepository : set_pre_render_cost_estimate_usd

AllocationPendingTickProcessor ..> AllocationPlanningService : plan_initial (heuristic only)
RetryExecutor ..> AllocationPlanningService : plan_retry (heuristic only)
AllocationPlanningService --> PgJobs : stamps estimated_cost_usd (heuristic)

AllocationFacade --> RenderGroupRepository : get_pre_render_cost_estimate_usd
AllocationFacade --> AllocationPlanningService : cost_for_committed_jobs(rows, snapshot_usd)

RenderGroupRepository --> PgRenderGroups : SELECT / UPDATE new column
DbInit --> PgRenderGroups : ALTER TABLE ADD COLUMN

' ============================================================
' Notes
' ============================================================
note bottom of RenderGroupService
  Why call cost_for_dry_run a SECOND time at confirm
  instead of trusting whatever the client just saw?
    1. Server-driven -- no client/server trust gap.
    2. Cache hit -- the formula already lives in
       allocation_cost_file_formulas from the
       pre-render call moments earlier, so this is
       a DB read + math, not an LLM API call.
    3. Deterministic -- same heaviness + same
       safety_multiplier always yields the same
       number, so what we stamp matches what the
       UI showed.
end note

note bottom of AllocationPlanningService
  ``cost_for_committed_jobs`` is now snapshot-aware.
  Per-fleet breakdown (the per-chunk machines list the
  UI displays) still comes from rows -- only the
  ``total_cost_usd`` is overridden by the snapshot.
  This keeps the chunk-detail surface working with
  no changes elsewhere.
end note

note bottom of PgRenderGroups
  Frozen at submit.  Retries deliberately do NOT
  update this column -- the snapshot represents
  "what the user was quoted", which is the source
  of truth for billing-fairness comparisons.  Live
  cost (telemetry-driven) is separate and shown
  alongside.
end note

note bottom of allocation_time_analyzer
  The ``llm_base_seconds_at_anchor`` override field
  STAYS on the heaviness contract because
  cost_for_dry_run still uses it on the pre-render
  path.  The render flow (plan_initial / plan_retry)
  passes heaviness through without that field, so
  the analyzer runs the heuristic exactly as before.
end note

note bottom of AllocationFacade
  Read-path branch:
    snapshot != NULL  -> return snapshot value
                          (LLM-derived, what the
                          user was quoted)
    snapshot == NULL  -> SUM(jobs.estimated_cost_usd)
                          (legacy / heuristic --
                          covers groups submitted
                          before this column existed)
end note

@enduml
